# Dependencies resolve from the public npm registry (package-lock.json).
#
# Behind a corporate npm registry or mirror, point your own npm at it, in your user config
# rather than in this file:
#   npm config set registry https://npm.example.com/
#
# Behind a proxy that re-signs TLS, npm fails with SELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN or "unable to get
# local issuer certificate". Point npm at your company's CA bundle:
#   npm config set cafile /path/to/corporate-ca.pem
# or export NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/to/corporate-ca.pem
# Never set strict-ssl=false: it would accept any certificate, on every install, CI included.
